cxd3778gf: hold the codec mutex only inside one read()/write() of a table node

/proc/icx_audio_cxd3778gf_data/* took the codec's global mutex on the call at offset 0 and
released it only on the call that reached the end of the table. A partial read (head -c), a short
write, or a process killed in between left volume, PCM open and standby blocked until a restart
(seen 2026-09-29). A write that started at a non-zero offset used a NULL buffer, and every full
read printed the whole table to the kernel log at info level. Now each call locks and unlocks,
each open file gathers its own write, and the table is applied under the mutex once the whole
table and its checksum have arrived. dacdat's own use (write the whole file, read to EOF) is
unchanged.

